  "implementation": [
    "Ordinary Context owns the existing private NativeDevice. Loader/instance/device creation and destruction no longer have a duplicated route implementation. Native handles, selected queue and enabled storage-update-after-bind facts come from that owner; route PFNs are loaded once.",
    "HYLE native submission, exceptional queue drain and expert callbacks use the upstream device-submit then queue-handle locks. Normal admission uses a private raw callback/state overload, without constructing std::function or allocating a hot dispatch node. Native device loss observed in this queue seam poisons the provider runtime.",
    "Borrowed buffers request an address only when their caller explicitly proves address usage/allocation eligibility. Ordinary public storage/transfer buffers remain valid descriptor-based resident inputs.",
    "Existing route Buffer/Run/Completion ownership, actual memory quota, cancellation/close and retained results remain in use; no new global pending queue or per-kernel vtable was introduced."
  ],
