  "correctness_contract": {
    "ordinary_bridge": "An ordinary HYLE Neg Program produces a 17x2048 tensor. The exact same instance/device/queue imports this storage into an actual upstream RMSNorm region with epsilon 1e-6. Ordinary HYLE download verifies independent double arithmetic at 6e-6*(1+abs(expected)); a borrowed result retains native graph storage after releasing NativeGraph and after Context.close, then quota returns to zero.",
    "bridge_qualification": "The middle region is invoked through the private NativeGraph/NativeWork seam. This proves actual same-device resource interoperability, not ordinary managed Program/Graph coverage.",
    "existing_behavior": "All existing Vulkan Compute/Graph tests ran on the newly shared device owner, including tensor dtype/layout domains, liveness/views, changing inputs and two slots, result ownership, native OOM/observation/drain, cancellation/close and concurrent producers.",
    "expert_failure": "A throwing expert callback becomes Internal; the shared queue lock is released and subsequent native access/upload/download succeed.",
    "static_shared_difference": "The existing Graph MetadataAllocationFailureResetsReportAndLeaksNoDeviceStorage test is compiled only for HYLE_STATIC and no Tracy; its executable-local allocation interceptor cannot qualify a DLL allocation site. Shared runs 13 Graph cases, static 14; neither run skips a compiled test.",
    "shared_boundary": "Ordinary Context/Program/Graph and private NativeDevice/NativeGraph/NativeWork exercise HYLE DLLs in shared mode. Existing private PFN failure cases use the vendor copy linked into the test executable; the C host OOM fixture includes the identical patched allocator source with test-local allocator/symbol renaming.",
    "validation": "All final logs have no VUID or validation error; explicit validation enabled, required HYLE DLLs staged beside EXEs, runtime PATH unset.",
    "weights": "Generated numeric fixtures; actual checkpoint-weight acceptance remains Y4."
  },
  "retained_failure": [
    "The inherited developer build caches initially had WERROR=OFF. Their passing results were not promoted to the selector strict compile gate; final validation explicitly enables WERROR.",
    "MSVC deprecated getenv use in two existing private fixture paths was replaced with owned Windows CRT reads before the strict build.",
    "The first strict build rejected the test-only included vendor C source: missing UTF-8 on that C translation unit and its unchanged, deliberately masked FP16 conversion. The source gets /utf-8; warning 4244 is scoped only around the original vendor include. All HYLE warnings remain errors; vendor algorithms and source authentication are unchanged."
  ],
  "p0": {
    "cold_cost": "One existing upstream native runtime per ordinary Context; route duplicates of loader/instance/device creation are removed. Environment/PFN discovery is cold. This introduces full upstream device preparation into ordinary Context; no cold-start speedup is claimed.",
    "execution_cost": "Native submit acquires the original upstream queue locks using a stack callback/state record. No std::function construction, provider search, timing, additional pending container or kernel dispatch layer. Existing native command recording/rebinding remains unchanged.",
    "p1": "NOT_RUN: full C1-Y managed Direct/Graph, ordinary lifecycle integration and the qualified final candidate remain incomplete."
  },
